Jenkins Plugin Installation (Nautilus DevOps)
This guide documents the successful installation and configuration of the required core plugins (Git and GitLab) on the Nautilus DevOps Jenkins server to enable seamless CI/CD pipeline integration.

📋 Task Objectives
Access the Jenkins UI using provided administrator credentials (admin / Adm!n321).

Navigate to the Plugin Manager and ensure the Git plugin and GitLab Plugin are installed.

Restart Jenkins cleanly via the Update Centre option once installation is complete and no active jobs are running.

Verify functionality post-restart by re-authenticating and confirming active plugin status.

🛠️ Execution Steps
Step 1: Authentication & Access
Navigated to the Jenkins management interface via the top bar.

Logged in successfully with:

Username: admin

Password: Adm!n321

Step 2: Plugin Management & Installation
Navigated to Manage Jenkins ➔ Plugins ➔ Installed plugins / Available plugins.

Selected and verified the installation of:

Git plugin (Version 5.11.0)

GitLab Plugin (Version 1.9.13)

Step 3: Server Restart
Opted for the safe restart configuration: "Restart Jenkins when installation is complete and no jobs are running".

Waited for the server to cycle and the login page to reappear.

Re-authenticated to confirm all system states and plugin registrations were successfully saved.

